  "body": "As far as I can tell a JS `SharedArrayBuffer` can enter IDL through an IDL `ArrayBuffer` that's effectively a pointer to the JS object.\r\n\r\nNow assuming #342 is fixed and you can use `[AllowShared] ArrayBuffer` as return value, what language do you use to return a `SharedArrayBuffer`? Do you need to construct the JS object, then make an IDL `ArrayBuffer` object that points to it, and then return the IDL object?",
